14-## Contract
15-
16-**Runtime**
17-
18-One long-running service: the TanStack Start web app in `app/`, SSR. It serves both pages and server
19-functions; there is no separate API process. "Start the product" means the Vite dev server on the
20-fixed main port recorded in `.intentfold/project.json`.
21-
22-The database is remote: the shared Supabase project, schema `lemmadeck-schema`, reached through
23:`LEMMADECK_DATABASE_URL`. There is no local database. Content generation (`ld-s10y-lesson`,
24:`ld-s10y-image`, `ld-s10y-answer`, `sr-story`, `sr-voa1500`, `ld-galaxy`) runs as one-off scripts,
25-not as a service. Their committed resource inputs and outputs live under `ssot-resources/`;
26-rebuildable working files live under `.tmp/` and may be removed after the run.
27-
28-**Environments**
29-
30-One environment: **production**, hosted on Render. There is no staging or preview environment.
31-Render builds the root `Dockerfile` with the repo root as context, installing the standalone
32-project in `app/` and shipping only `app/.output`. Production remains a single always-on instance.
33-
--
41-**Evidence**
42-
43-Acceptance verification is acceptance-criteria only. A ticket proves its own criteria against an
44:authoritative surface and stops; no regression pass is added to the flow.
45-
46-Evidence must be reproducible and capable of failing. Use the smallest observation that settles the
47:criterion: a command, query, or browser interaction. Code inspection alone is not evidence that
48-behavior works.
49-
50-A ticket-scoped browser check is a command-line script under
51-`.intentfold/tickets/<ticket-id>/tmp/`, uncommitted. One script covering all criteria is the normal
52-case, with a screenshot per visual criterion. `app/tests/` remains the project's long-lived
53-Playwright suite and is not where ticket-scoped checks live.
54-
55:`playwright-cli open <url>` is useful for debugging but is never acceptance evidence. A criterion
56-check asserts the reachable page or flow, required controls and regions, accepted action, correctly
57-placed result, resolved loading state, absence of an error-only state, and the expected value shape.
58-
59-A chore's proof is whatever settles its criterion. When the criterion is visible only in the running
60-product, verify it there even when a query proves the underlying row exists.
61-
