239-**Environment troubleshooting.** A missing `app/.env` symlink appears as the app starting while every
240-DB-backed page fails. Recreate the symlink rather than copying `.env`.
241-
242:**Choose authoritative evidence.** A database query proves a row exists but not that the UI shows
243-it. A browser proves rendered behavior but may not prove a background write completed. Use both only
244-when the criterion spans both surfaces.
245-
246-**Use headed browser verification for formal UI acceptance.** Fall back to headless only when no GUI
247-is available and record that limitation.
248-
249-**Drive a real browser from a script.** An embedded preview pane can produce false negatives for
250-lazy-loading and viewport logic. It may demonstrate a page to the human, but it is not acceptance
251:evidence.
252-
253-**Use stable locators.** Prefer role, label, placeholder, visible text, or a stable `data-testid`.
254-Locate the stable container first, then assert its contents. Do not locate by CSS class chains or DOM
255-structure invisible to the user.
256-
257-**Treat generated content as dynamic.** Assert completion, placement, non-empty output, and shape
258-rather than exact generated wording. Wait for a completion signal or stable text, and ensure stale
259-content cannot satisfy a new action's assertion.
260-
--
271-**Authentication failures stop operations.** A cloud command failing authentication is a stop for
272-human re-authentication, not a reason to retry with a different account, workspace, or subscription.
273-
274:## Redlines
275-
276-1. **Recording a criterion as passed when its check did not run** — forbidden outright. An
277-   environment or external limit that stopped the run is recorded exactly as it happened.
278-2. **Writing to the real learner's data from a test** — forbidden outright. Tests use
279-   `sr_users.id = 2`, never `sr_users.id = 1`.
280-3. **Driving `https://lemmadeck.com` during acceptance** — forbidden outright. Signing in, clicking,
281-   submitting, or any other write-capable interaction is prohibited; acceptance runs against
282-   localhost. A read-only GET required by the post-deploy check is allowed.
283-4. **Writing a real password, session secret, or DB connection string into a check script, ticket
